+
+Cartesian closure of $\mathbf{TeleoSh}(M)$, asserted in Chapter 1, is verified by constructing the exponential object $Y^X$ for objects $X, Y$ of $\mathbf{TeleoSh}(M)$ as the sheafification, in the sense of Book 17's Chapter 5, of the presheaf assigning to each open $U$ the set of morphisms $X|_U \to Y|_U$, following the standard construction of exponentials in a sheaf topos and confirming the resulting object satisfies the required universal property with respect to the product constructed from Book 15's tensor product.
